+### Issue 2: CRITICAL - Badge Colors Wrong (Lines 860-861)
+
+**Problem:**
+The inline style attribute was overriding CSS class selectors with wrong colors:
+- TR: `#fff59d` (yellow) ❌ → Should be: `#4a9eff` (blue)
+- BÖLGE: `#c5e1a5` (green) ❌ → Should be: `#ff9800` (orange)
+
+The inline styles completely bypassed the CSS variable system defined in styles.css.
+
+**Fix Applied:**
+Removed all inline style attributes and let CSS class selectors handle colors:
+
+```javascript
+// BEFORE
+<span class="selection-badge" data-status="${status}" style="background: ${status === 'TR' ? '#fff59d' : status === 'BÖLGE' ? '#c5e1a5' : '#f0f0f0'}; ...">
+
+// AFTER
+<span class="selection-badge" data-status="${badgeStatus}">
+    ${athlete.selected_slot || '-'}
+</span>
+```
+
+**Color Mapping (CSS):**
+- `data-status="TR"` → `--badge-tr: #4a9eff` (blue) ✓
+- `data-status="BÖLGE"` → `--badge-bolge: #ff9800` (orange) ✓
+- `data-status="MULTINATIONS"` → `--badge-multi: #9c27b0` (purple) ✓
+- `data-status="BARAJ_YOK"` → `--badge-baraj: #999` (gray) ✓
+
+**Impact:** Badges now display correct colors per specification. Dark mode also works correctly with CSS variable overrides.
+
+---
+
+### Issue 3: IMPORTANT - Multinations Badge Color Missing
+
+**Problem:**
+Multinations athletes showed the ⭐ star in the name column, but the selection badge didn't reflect multinations status. The badge would show "TR" or "BÖLGE" color instead of purple.
+
+**Fix Applied:**
+Create badgeStatus variable that checks multinations flag before selection status:
+
+```javascript
+// BEFORE
+const status = getSelectionBadgeStatus(athlete.selected);
+
+// AFTER
+const badgeStatus = athlete.multinations ? 'MULTINATIONS' : (athlete.selected || 'BARAJ_YOK');
+```
+
+Then pass badgeStatus to the badge:
+```javascript
+<span class="selection-badge" data-status="${badgeStatus}">
+```
+
+**Impact:** Multinations athletes now show purple badges regardless of TR/BÖLGE selection status. Single badge clearly indicates athlete status.
+
